UPDATE care_chart_week_content SET move = $movejson${"format":"sections","theme":"Small daily identity moments","mantra":"You are still allowed to be a person, not only a role.","reset":"360° Breathing, five rounds","today":"20 minutes of your choice","build":["Reverse Lunge, 10 per side","Incline Push-Up, 10 reps","Bird Dog, 8 per side"],"release":"A stretch of your choice","door":null,"exercise":{"name":"A session done purely for you","focus":"movement as one of the small identity moments itself","benefit":"This session doesn't need to serve your toddler, your household, or anyone else's schedule — it can simply be yours.","mistake":"Framing every action, including this one, around its usefulness to your family.","tip":"Notice, just once today, that this is happening because you wanted it, not because it was required."},"inRealLife":"A whole person, not just a role, is allowed to be the point of today.","why":"Small, unremarkable daily moments — a song you like, five minutes with a book, a session like this one — quietly keep your own identity alive alongside motherhood, not instead of it.","quote":null,"note":null,"safety":"Same core guidance as always — consistency over intensity. Stop for pain, new leaking or heaviness, joint pain that doesn't ease, or anything that feels wrong.","recovery":["A sense of self outside of 'mother' today","Mood generally steady","Physical strength continuing to feel solid","Some real enjoyment in something just for you"],"reflectionPrompt":null,"closingLabel":"Notice this","closingText":"however small today's moment of 'just you' was, it counted, for its own sake.","lookingAhead":"Over the next week, it's worth watching what values you're actually modeling, not just stating.","milestone":null,"breathLegacy":null,"philosophy":null,"finalNote":null,"signatureLine":null,"childLearned":null,"whatYouGaveYourself":null,"tiers":null,"recoveryRoute":null,"progressionNote":null,"move":null,"clinicalFlag":null}$movejson$::jsonb WHERE week_number = 146;
UPDATE care_chart_week_content SET move = $movejson${"format":"sections","theme":"What they're absorbing","mantra":"Children learn enormously through watching, not only through what they're told.","reset":"360° Breathing, five rounds","today":"20 minutes of your choice","build":["Step-Up, 10 per side","Standing Row (light band), 10 reps","Glute Bridge March, 10 per side"],"release":"A stretch of your choice","door":null,"exercise":{"name":"Whatever movement feels honest today","focus":"movement as one small, ordinary example among many","benefit":"Showing up for yourself, honestly and without drama, is one small example among the many things a young child is absorbing from daily life.","mistake":"Assuming any single day carries outsized weight in what a child learns.","tip":"Let today's session simply be honest — no need to perform anything for anyone."},"inRealLife":"At this age, children learn enormously through watching and imitating the people around them — not only through what they're told.","why":"At this age (roughly two to two-and-a-half), children learn enormously through watching and imitating the people around them — not only through what they're explicitly told. That's a real, gentle fact, not a reason to perform.","quote":null,"note":null,"safety":"Same core guidance as always — consistency over intensity. Stop for pain, new leaking or heaviness, joint pain that doesn't ease, or anything that feels wrong.","recovery":["A clear sense of the values you actually hold","Mood generally steady","Physical strength continuing to feel solid","No pressure to perform anything today"],"reflectionPrompt":null,"closingLabel":"A gentle fact","closingText":"however today's session looked, it didn't need to be a lesson for anyone. It could just be yours.","lookingAhead":"Next week, it's worth reconnecting with a personal passion or hobby that's been quiet for a while.","milestone":null,"breathLegacy":null,"philosophy":null,"finalNote":null,"signatureLine":null,"childLearned":null,"whatYouGaveYourself":null,"tiers":null,"recoveryRoute":null,"progressionNote":null,"move":null,"clinicalFlag":null}$movejson$::jsonb WHERE week_number = 147;
UPDATE care_chart_week_content SET move = $movejson${"format":"sections","theme":"A quiet passion, returned to","mantra":"Whatever you loved before motherhood is still allowed to matter.","reset":"360° Breathing, five rounds","today":"20 minutes of your choice","build":["Lateral Band Walk, 10 per side","Half-Kneeling Press, 8 per side","Calf Raise, 15 reps"],"release":"A stretch of your choice","door":null,"exercise":{"name":"Movement borrowed from an old hobby or interest, if one applies","focus":"reconnecting with a personal interest through movement","benefit":"If dance, sport, or another physical hobby mattered to you before motherhood, borrowing from it today is a real, gentle way back in.","mistake":"Assuming an old passion is permanently gone rather than simply dormant.","tip":"Let today's movement nod toward something you genuinely used to love."},"inRealLife":"An old interest, picked back up even briefly, belongs to you, full stop — it doesn't need to justify itself to anyone.","why":"Interests set aside during the most intense early years aren't gone — they're simply waiting for a little more bandwidth, which this stage often finally offers.","quote":null,"note":null,"safety":"Same core guidance as always — consistency over intensity. Stop for pain, new leaking or heaviness, joint pain that doesn't ease, or anything that feels wrong.","recovery":["Some sense of reconnecting with a personal interest","Mood generally steady","Physical strength continuing to feel solid","A sense of a fuller identity than 'just mother'"],"reflectionPrompt":null,"closingLabel":"Worth celebrating","closingText":"however small today's reconnection with an old interest was, it mattered simply because it was yours.","lookingAhead":"Next week is for the mother who still doesn't feel entirely like herself — and that's worth naming directly.","milestone":null,"breathLegacy":null,"philosophy":null,"finalNote":null,"signatureLine":null,"childLearned":null,"whatYouGaveYourself":null,"tiers":null,"recoveryRoute":null,"progressionNote":null,"move":null,"clinicalFlag":null}$movejson$::jsonb WHERE week_number = 148;
UPDATE care_chart_week_content SET move = $movejson${"format":"sections","theme":"\"What if I still don't feel like myself?\"","mantra":"There is no deadline for becoming yourself again.","reset":"360° Breathing, five rounds","today":"15-20 minutes, whatever feels manageable today","build":["360° Breathing, extra rounds","Whatever movement feels genuinely okay today","Rest, if that's what's actually needed"],"release":"A stretch of your choice, or none at all","door":null,"exercise":{"name":"Whatever today can honestly hold","focus":"no pressure to have arrived anywhere by now","benefit":"There's no requirement to feel fully like 'yourself' again by any particular week — this practice works exactly the same whether or not you do.","mistake":"Assuming something is wrong if you don't feel recognisably like your old self by now.","tip":"Let today's movement, whatever it is, exist without needing to prove anything about how healed or 'found' you are."},"inRealLife":"You don't owe anyone, including yourself, a fully reassembled identity on any particular timeline.","why":"For some mothers, two to two-and-a-half years in still doesn't feel like enough time to feel fully like themselves again — and that's genuinely, completely okay. There's no deadline here. It's also worth considering that the goal was never to become the exact person you were before. Whoever you're becoming instead is allowed to still be unclear, still forming, still a work in progress. That isn't behind schedule. That's just honest.","quote":null,"note":"If \"I don't feel like myself\" has come with persistent sadness, numbness, or a sense of disconnection that worries you, that's worth a real conversation with your care provider — not something to just wait out.","safety":"Consistency over intensity, still. Stop and seek care for pain above 4/10, new leaking or pelvic heaviness with exercise, joint pain that doesn't ease with rest, or anything that feels wrong. Persistent low mood, anxiety, or intrusive thoughts deserve real support at any point.","recovery":["Some honesty about where you actually are, without judgment","A sense of who to talk to if this feeling has weighed heavily","Physical health feeling stable","Permission to still be figuring this out"],"reflectionPrompt":"If you're not fully back to your old self, what would it mean to stop waiting to be — and just meet whoever you're becoming instead?","closingLabel":"A gentle fact","closingText":"however close or far today felt from 'yourself,' there was no deadline you missed.","lookingAhead":"Over the next week, it's worth doing a full, honest check of everything your body can now do.","milestone":null,"breathLegacy":null,"philosophy":null,"finalNote":null,"signatureLine":null,"childLearned":null,"whatYouGaveYourself":null,"tiers":null,"recoveryRoute":null,"progressionNote":null,"move":null,"clinicalFlag":null}$movejson$::jsonb WHERE week_number = 149;
