UPDATE care_chart_week_content SET move = $movejson${"format":"sections","theme":"The third birthday","mantra":"You did not just get through three years. You built a life within them.","reset":"360° Breathing, five rounds","today":"20 minutes of your choice, or however you'd like to mark this week","build":["Whichever movements feel most meaningful to you today"],"release":"360° Breathing, as long as feels good","door":{"pattern":"Carry","comfort":"Suitcase Carry (light), 2 trips per side","steady":"Farmer Carry, 2-3 trips per side","challenge":"Farmer Carry (heavier or longer), 3+ trips per side"},"exercise":{"name":"360° Breathing (final marker)","focus":"the one practice that has outlasted the entire journey","benefit":"Every single exercise in this whole three-year journey has changed, progressed, or been replaced. This alone hasn't.","mistake":"None — there's no wrong way to do this today.","tip":"Just breathe, wide and unhurried, exactly the same way you did in week one of pregnancy."},"inRealLife":"This breath has now been with you through pregnancy, birth, healing, rebuilding, an entire first year, a full second year, and a full third year — it will keep being useful for as long as you need it, long after this programme ends.","why":"Three years ago, this journey began with a body just learning it was pregnant, and a breath that had no idea yet how far it would travel. Today, that same body has grown, delivered, healed, rebuilt, settled into strength, chosen its own rhythm across two full years, and spent this final year asking a harder, quieter question: who are you becoming? This week doesn't need a new answer. It needs only an honest look at everything true so far.","quote":null,"note":null,"safety":"Consistency over intensity, still. Stop and seek care for pain above 4/10, new leaking or pelvic heaviness with exercise, joint pain that doesn't ease with rest, or anything that feels wrong. Persistent low mood, anxiety, or intrusive thoughts deserve real support at any point.","recovery":["A genuine sense of three full years of real change","Physical strength and stamina both meaningfully built","Mood steady, or supported if it isn't","Real trust in your own body and your own judgment, earned over three whole years"],"reflectionPrompt":"Three years on from week one — who are you now, and how does that compare to who you thought you'd become?","closingLabel":"Worth celebrating","closingText":"you did not just survive three years. You built real strength, real autonomy, and a real, whole life within them — on your own timeline, the entire way through, for reasons that were always allowed to be your own.","lookingAhead":"This is the end of the structured programme. What comes next is entirely, genuinely yours to shape.","milestone":"Three years ago, you were just beginning to meet each other. Today, you know each other completely, and you are both still becoming.","breathLegacy":"The breath that carried you through pregnancy, birth, and three full years of motherhood will keep carrying you through everything still ahead — with or without a programme telling you to use it.","philosophy":"There was never anything to catch up to. There was only ever the next step, whenever you were ready. There still is.","finalNote":"This programme is ending. You are not required to keep any part of it. If 360° Breathing, or a squat, or a Tuesday session becomes part of your life for years to come, that's wonderful. If none of it does, everything it gave you while it lasted was still real and still yours. Whatever comes next — for your child, and separately, for you — was never something this programme needed to decide. That was always yours to shape.","signatureLine":["You were never trying to get your body back.","You were meeting the woman you were becoming — one breath at a time."],"childLearned":["Grieved honestly, and stayed proud anyway.","Held boundaries, patience, and rest as ongoing practices, not lessons once learned.","Trusted a body that changed, healed, and kept going.","Kept asking who she was becoming, long after the easy answers ran out."],"whatYouGaveYourself":["Three years of a practice that was never about becoming someone else's idea of a good mother.","A body you trust, built through real, honest effort, on your own terms.","Permission to rest, to want more, to grieve, and to be proud, all without needing anyone's approval.","A whole life that includes, but was never only about, motherhood."],"tiers":null,"recoveryRoute":null,"progressionNote":null,"move":null,"clinicalFlag":null}$movejson$::jsonb WHERE week_number = 196;
